  <readme><![CDATA[
# Ollama — Local LLM Daemon

Unlike every other CBE provider, Ollama is **not** a hosted chat service —
it's a local daemon you run on your own machine. There is no signup, no
website to sign in to, and no rate limit beyond what your GPU/CPU can
chew through. The "URL" `http://127.0.0.1:11434` is the local HTTP API
the daemon exposes; the bridge talks to it directly over JSON, no
browser involved.

**First-time setup:**

  1. Install Ollama from [ollama.com/download](https://ollama.com/download)
     (Windows / macOS / Linux native installers).
  2. Open a terminal and `ollama pull llama3.2` (or any model you want).
  3. The daemon auto-starts on `127.0.0.1:11434`; CBE discovers
     installed models via `GET /api/tags`.

**Models typically exposed** (whatever you've `ollama pull`'d):

  - llama3.2 (1B / 3B / 11B / 90B) — Meta's general-purpose
  - qwen2.5 / qwen2.5-coder — Alibaba open-weights
  - mistral / mixtral — Mistral AI open-weights
  - phi3 / phi3.5 — Microsoft small-but-mighty
  - deepseek-r1 — open reasoning weights

**Privacy:** 100% local. No prompt, response, or model weight ever leaves
your machine. Ideal for sensitive code or air-gapped work.
  ]]></readme>

